{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>El</b> — Let him pray in the name of HaShem that He not kill them for even one moment, lest my people forget the deeds of HaShem against the wicked." "<b>They wander</b> — to seek bread, as he mentioned concerning dogs; they wander about to eat." "The sense of <b>by Your strength</b> — they are Israel." "<b>And bring them down</b> — from the height of their wealth." "<b>Our shield</b> — He is our king in truth, an allusion, on account of Saul the king who ordered him put to death."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:17.139530610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}